abstract: >-
  spexial provides special functions for JAX, following the
  scipy.special API. The implementations are written in terms
  of JAX primitives, so they compose with jit compilation,
  automatic differentiation and vectorisation, and run on CPU,
  GPU and TPU. spexial fills gaps in jax.scipy.special, which
  has no modified Bessel K functions at any release and returns
  nan for zeta on the negative real line, and supplies analytic
  derivatives that cut backward-pass memory by up to 268x. A few
  routines also reach further than their scipy counterparts:
  the exponentially scaled Bessel functions stay accurate to
  DBL_MAX, where scipy.special.kve returns nan, and the complex
  Spence function is correct at 3 +/- sqrt(3), where scipy loses
  every significant digit. Several routines originate in the LINX
  code, and the complex Spence function is translated from
  scipy's Cython implementation.
keywords:
